Speaking to <a href="https://www.billboard.com/pro/zane-lowe-interviewing-stars-growing-apple-music-radio/"><em>Billboard</em></a>, Lowe said the audience is expanding rapidly, 11 years after the service debuted as "Beats 1."<br/>
<br/>
Lowe arrived from BBC Radio 1 and said he expected his existing relationships, combined with Apple's resources and Jimmy Iovine's backing, to generate interest. But with the station yet to establish itself, "it was kind of crickets."<br/>
<br/>
Booking difficulties helped steer Apple's programming toward less established performers. Billie Eilish, Khalid, and Bryson Tiller were among the artists it supported as their careers began. This year, the network has broadcast music by more than 6,500 artists, over half of whom Lowe described as new or emerging. Lowe also disclosed that some recorded interviews have never been released because the artists subsequently approached him with concerns.<br/>
<br/>
